{
  "headline": "Carboplatin shortage persists 42 months after FDA first posted it, linked to Intas OAI inspection and import alerts",
  "headline_cites": ["E31", "D9", "E16", "E18", "E19"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the carboplatin shortage on 2023-04-28 and as of 2026-10-21 it has been on the shortage list for 42 months.",
      "cites": ["E31", "D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An FDA inspection of Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited (FEI 3004011473) ended 2022-12-02 and was classified OAI, with the classification letter dated 2023-04-05, 23 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E16", "D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Import alert 66-40 for Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited was published 2023-06-01 and again 2023-11-14, and a Warning Letter was issued 2023-07-28.",
      "cites": ["E18", "E19", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Multiple manufacturers remain in current shortage status per FDA, including Accord Healthcare (supplied by Intas), Teva, Fresenius Kabi, Hospira/Pfizer, Eugia, Gland Pharma, Avyxa, and Teyro Labs.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E22", "E24", "E25", "E26", "E27", "E28", "E29"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds two carboplatin products: NDC 00703423901 (Teva, manufactured by Pharmachemie BV) with 54 units on hand and NDC 60505628201 (Apotex, manufactured by Teyro Labs) with 77 units on hand.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E9", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale Lakeside has only 4 units on hand at 2.1 per day (2 days supply) while Corvale East has 131 units at 7.3 per day (18 days supply).",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "P&T has approved interchange between the Teva and Apotex products (same product, alternate manufacturer) and between Accord and Teva (same molecule, alternate concentration or vial size).",
      "cites": ["E32", "E33"]
    }
  ]
}
